  "question": {
    "text": "An equilateral prism of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> rests on a rough horizontal surface, with a coefficient of friction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>μ</mi></math>. A horizontal force&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math> is applied to the prism, as shown in the figure. If the coefficient of friction is sufficiently high, so that the prism does not slide before toppling, then the minimum force required to topple the prism is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0017_3aed630ade39.jpg\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 130px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>",
