  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The prism will topple after&nbsp;normal reaction shifts to the rightmost part of the prism.</p><p>Hence, at that time, equating torque about the toppling point ( rightmost point of the prism) due to force&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math>&nbsp;and force due to gravity&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>×</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math><br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0017_db4900bb75cc.jpg\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 129px;\" /></p>"
  }
